{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs at b3bf30833b93aaec5fc3adab7ffa0b6f0fe7792d. Nine pages are re-anchored onto the merged kernel and app artifacts, so their predecessors can finally be retired.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. Seven stranded identifiers collapse to two. Pages citing the internal/kernel predecessors d97eed89, 45f88594 and 9999be33 now cite 61bafadb; pages citing the internal/app predecessors 82a33e46, 0ea5a63a and 845e3cc9 now cite 1555aaee. The nine pages are README.md, why.md, concepts/components.md, how-to/deploy-a-resident.md, how-to/end-to-end.md, reference/architecture.md, reference/gs/serve.md, reference/gs/status.md and reference/limits.md. limits.md loses a line, because two of its citations resolved to the same successor.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. Merge 126c9408 changed internal/kernel and internal/app, so step five wants their artifacts superseded. I could not do that at merge time: retiring a cited artifact is fatal to the citation gate, and d97eed89 alone is cited by eight pages. Retiring them then would have turned main red on landing, which is the failure that has already cost a repair merge and two rejected heads today. The retirement and the re-anchoring have to travel together, and this head is the re-anchoring half. With it merged, the predecessors can be withdrawn without breaking anything.\n\nPROSE IS UNCHANGED, AND THAT IS A CONCLUSION RATHER THAN AN OMISSION. These pages now assert their claims hold at the merge commit, where the kernel gained a bounded submission queue, so a blind citation swap would have been the exact failure I made this morning on five other pages. I checked instead: every claim these pages make about the sequencer is that it sequences concurrent appends, which a bound on in-flight submissions does not alter, and none of them says the queue is unbounded. The bound is documented in limits.md, where limits belong, and duplicating it elsewhere would create a second place to get it wrong.\n\nSELF-INITIATED, so there is no request, promise or report — the discipline says a commitment loop between one actor and itself keeps no promise the log needs. The implementing commit rests on 61bafadb, the kernel merge artifact, which is what motivates the work: it states plainly that succession at that path is incomplete and why. The tradeoff is that nothing shows this as in-flight on the board until now.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DO. It does not retire anything. The predecessors stay live until this head merges, and three of them — 9999be33, 845e3cc9 and 00c6eefb — are codex's and need their author regardless. I have twice today written that a retirement happened when the fold had refused it, so the retirements are deliberately left to the merge step and will be verified from the fold rather than from my intent.\n\nGATES at this exact head: internal/docset uncached 81.457s, make docs 83.051s, git diff --check clean, git merge-tree against main 126c9408 clean.\n\nRests on the live non-stale docs predecessor 37e77cf5 at the merge commit, and on the two artifacts the pages now cite.","body":{"commit":"b3bf30833b93aaec5fc3adab7ffa0b6f0fe7792d","path":"docs"}}